        Case(
            "longest talk kubecon-cloudnativecon-north-america-2026:1362599",
            "Demo Theater: YugabyteDB AMP: Agentic Multitenant PostgreSQL for the AI Era\u000AAI agents are bursty, mostly idle, and unpredictable at scale. Traditional databases charge you for idle capacity and buckle when one runaway agent hogs shared resources. Yet AI agents still need high availability, resilience, and constant tuning, and the ones that reach production often outgrow a single node.\u000AYugabyteDB AMP (Agentic Multitenant Postgres) is built for that journey. It manages large database fleets, each growing from a fraction of a core to a distributed, multi-continent deployment, with no migration or re-architecture along the way.\u000AJoin the YugabyteDB team for a first look at AMP. You\u2019ll learn:\u000AHow to spin up PostgreSQL clusters with an agent, MCP, the API, or the UI, and branch onto independent compute with zero-copy thin cloning\u000AHow AMP\u2019s idle databases scale to zero, so small and early-stage workloads don't pay for idle capacity \u000AHow four agents (Architect, Voyager, Perf Advisor, and Nexus) automate setup, migration, integrations, and performance tuning\u000A\u000A_In order to facilitate networking and business relationships at the event, you may choose to visit a third party\u2019s booth or access sponsored content. You are never required to visit third party booths or to access sponsored content. When visiting a booth or participating in sponsored activities, the third party will receive some of your registration data. This data includes your first name, last name, title, company, address, email, standard demographics questions (i.e. job function, industry), and details about the sponsored content or resources you interacted with. If you choose to interact with a booth or access sponsored content, you are explicitly consenting to receipt and use of such data by the third-party recipients, which will be subject to their own privacy policies._",
