        Case(
            "longest talk kubecon-cloudnativecon-north-america-2026:1362604",
            "Demo Theater: AI already found your Java vulnerabilities. Has your scanner?\u000AYour scanner says your Java dependencies are clean. It is wrong. A scanner only matches known CVEs, and some of the most dangerous vulnerabilities were never filed as one.\u000A\u000AMost teams are stuck on old versions, and it is worse than you think. Attackers now point AI at open-source code to find and exploit these bugs with or without a CVE, so a clean scan is no protection.\u000A\u000AChainguard Libraries for Java backports known-CVE fixes into source-built artifacts, so you remediate without a disruptive upgrade. Chainguard Athena stacks the silent bugs on top: the same AI, on defense, finds the bugs that never got a CVE and ships them fixed through the same artifacts.\u000A\u000AIn this live demo we take a Maven project with one of these silent bugs, confirm no scanner warns you, then switch to Chainguard Libraries and rebuild to see it remediated.\u000A\u000AUpgrading to the latest is still the real goal, and too often wishful thinking. AI finally makes doing it now realistic. Stop shipping vulnerable Java code.\u000A\u000A_In order to facilitate networking and business relationships at the event, you may choose to visit a third party\u2019s booth or access sponsored content. You are never required to visit third party booths or to access sponsored content. When visiting a booth or participating in sponsored activities, the third party will receive some of your registration data. This data includes your first name, last name, title, company, address, email, standard demographics questions (i.e. job function, industry), and details about the sponsored content or resources you interacted with. If you choose to interact with a booth or access sponsored content, you are explicitly consenting to receipt and use of such data by the third-party recipients, which will be subject to their own privacy policies._",
