        Case(
            "talk kubecon-cloudnativecon-north-america-2026:1331660",
            "Maintaining at Agent Speed with Hive Commons\u000AIn the last 90 days Hive Commons merged 5,292 pull requests across 433 releases in 17 repositories. 3,772 of them were opened by autonomous agents that triage the issue, write the fix, and merge through the same CI gates a human contributor faces. Five minutes on what that actually changes for a maintainer: what the agents handle well, what they consistently get wrong, and why the failures are almost never the code they write.",
            "101,8498,2012,4005,3177,2007,26736,7674,1999,1996,2197,3938,2420,26736,7674,5314,1019,1010,25797,4139,11186,2408,4724,2509,7085,1999,2459,16360,20049,29469,2229,1012,1017,1010,6255,2475,1997,2068,2020,2441,2011,8392,6074,2008,13012,4270,1996,3277,1010,4339,1996,8081,1010,1998,13590,2083,1996,2168,25022,6733,1037,2529,12130,5344,1012,2274,2781,2006,2054,2008,2941,3431,2005,1037,5441,2121,1024,2054,1996,6074,5047,2092,1010,2054,2027,10862,2131,3308,1010,1998,2339,1996,15428,2024,2471,2196,1996,3642,2027,4339,1012,102",
            102,
        ),
        Case(
            "talk kubecon-cloudnativecon-north-america-2026:1336104",
            "Translating Mesh Identity into MCP Impersonation: Governing AI Agent Identities with Istio\u000AEveryone is building an agentic platform right now, autonomous agents that choose their own tools and call real systems through MCP, often wearing your users\u2019 credentials. And every security team hits the same concern: how do you trust a workload whose next action you can\u2019t predict? Istio exists precisely to create trust between workloads that don\u2019t deserve the benefit of the doubt. This talk stretches those primitives over the agentic world: each agent becomes a first-class principal with its own SPIFFE identity. mTLS seals every hop from agent to gateway to tool. And at the MCP boundary, the AuthorizationPolicy decide, per request, which agent may invoke which tool on behalf of which user, leaving an audit trail that can prove it afterwards. Leave with a mental model for agents as workload identities rather than API-key holders, a reusable policy pattern for per-tool authorization, and an audit story that answers \u201Cwho acted, for whom, on what\u201D, whether you run one agent or a fleet.",
            "101,22969,20437,4767,2046,11338,2361,17727,18617,3370,1024,8677,9932,4005,15702,2007,21541,3695,3071,2003,2311,2019,4005,2594,4132,2157,2085,1010,8392,6074,2008,5454,2037,2219,5906,1998,2655,2613,3001,2083,11338,2361,1010,2411,4147,2115,5198,1521,22496,1012,1998,2296,3036,2136,4978,1996,2168,5142,1024,2129,2079,2017,3404,1037,2147,11066,3005,2279,2895,2017,2064,1521,1056,16014,1029,21541,3695,6526,10785,2000,3443,3404,2090,2147,11066,2015,2008,2123,1521,1056,10107,1996,5770,1997,1996,4797,1012,2023,2831,14082,2216,10968,2015,2058,1996,4005,2594,2088,1024,2169,4005,4150,1037,2034,1011,2465,4054,2007,2049,2219,11867,13355,2063,4767,1012,11047,4877,13945,2296,6154,2013,4005,2000,11909,2000,6994,1012,1998,2012,1996,11338,2361,6192,1010,1996,20104,18155,2594,2100,5630,1010,2566,5227,1010,2029,4005,2089,1999,6767,3489,2029,6994,2006,6852,1997,2029,5310,1010,2975,2019,15727,4446,2008,2064,6011,2009,5728,1012,2681,2007,1037,5177,2944,2005,6074,2004,2147,11066,15702,2738,2084,17928,1011,3145,13304,1010,1037,2128,10383,3468,3343,5418,2005,2566,1011,6994,20104,1010,1998,2019,15727,2466,2008,6998,1523,2040,6051,1010,2005,3183,1010,2006,2054,1524,1010,3251,2017,2448,2028,4005,2030,1037,4170,1012,102",
            235,
