        Case(
            "talk pytorch-day-japan-2026:1331879",
            "Accelerating PyTorch on Apple silicon\u000AAt the start of 2026, running models on PyTorch's MPS backend would mean working around unsupported operations, performance bottlenecks and memory growth even for small models. Since then, MPS has become much more mature platform to run the regular models on locally.\u000A\u000AThis talk goes through the progress on the backend such as, fused attention for prefill/decode workloads, Flex Attention, native Metal kernels for linear algebra operations, convolutions, porting MPS Graph to Metal kernels and memory allocator changes which fixes unexpected memory growth. I'll connect these changes to real model workloads from Hugging Face across language, image and video models, showing how improvements across the backend add up to better user experience.\u000A\u000AWe'll look at where MPS stands today, where are it's limitations compared to MLX and what are the upcoming changes we can expect for the backend in the near future.",
