        Case(
            "talk pytorch-day-japan-2026:1341807",
            "Training Robot Policies from Object Storage: LeRobot's Native LanceDB Backend\u000ALeRobot is Hugging Face's PyTorch library for real-world robotics, and its dataset format gave the community a shared standard. But robot learning data is multimodal and growing fast: long multi-camera videos, states, actions and language instructions in every episode. Training from object storage with global shuffling, and finding the right episodes first, still means copying data or stitching systems together.\u000A\u000ALanceDB and the LeRobot team upstreamed LanceDB as the first non-LeRobot storage backend. Users keep the familiar LeRobotDataset API and read Lance datasets in place from the Hub, HF buckets or S3.\u000A\u000AThis session covers:\u000A- How episodes, frames and videos are laid out as tables for random access\u000A- Feeding PyTorch: map-style datasets, global shuffle from object storage, and pitfalls with parallel workers\u000A- Using the same table to search, curate and train, with vector and full-text search\u000A- What it took to move from an external plugin into LeRobot core\u000A\u000AYou'll leave with steps to try in your own LeRobot setup, and a clear view of when this design helps and its current limits.",
