        Case(
            "talk pytorch-day-japan-2026:1343042",
            "From Learners to Contributors: Growing the PyTorch Ecosystem through PyTorchKR\u000AHow can a local PyTorch community turn learners into open-source contributors?\u000A\u000AThis talk shares lessons from eight years of PyTorch Korea, focusing on tutorials-kr, a community-maintained Korean translation of the official PyTorch tutorials. We explain how translated learning resources, university lectures, and open-source mentoring create entry points for developers, researchers, and students to contribute.\u000A\u000AOur mentoring efforts supported 26 first-time contributors and 51 merged PRs to tutorials-kr, which has welcomed more than 160 contributors overall. We use this experience to discuss lowering the barrier to a first contribution, supporting contributors through review, and connecting learning activities with open-source participation. We also share how the vLLM Korea Meetup broadened knowledge exchange across the PyTorch ecosystem.\u000A\u000AAttendees will leave with practical lessons for organizing contribution opportunities, connecting education with project maintenance, and measuring community reach and contribution outcomes separately.",
