            "talk pytorch-day-japan-2026:1343082",
            "DeepSpeed at the Frontier: Community-Driven Optimizations for State-of-the-Art Training Performance\u000ADeepSpeed is a pioneering distributed training framework built on top of PyTorch, combining performance and scalability with ease of use. It has over 43,000 GitHub stars and one million+ monthly PyPI downloads. DeepSpeed now delivers performance competitive with other state-of-the-art frameworks on frontier models, with just a configuration change. This talk presents the key recent optimizations and benchmark results.\u000ABest known for ZeRO, DeepSpeed has since added expert, sequence, and tensor parallelism (AutoEP, AutoSP, AutoTP) that compose with ZeRO and work with a wide range of models, including many Hugging Face models. Much of this progress has come from contributions by researchers and engineers across many organizations. AutoEP, for instance, brings optimized kernels and communication to large-scale MoE training, while DeepCompile optimizes communication scheduling and memory offloading at the compiler level using torch.compile. This success reflects DeepSpeed's open development, which draws a wide variety of contributions, including experimental and research-oriented features.",
