        Case(
            "talk pytorch-day-japan-2026:1343099",
            "OneComp: One-Command LLM Quantization\u000ADeploying large language models (LLMs) on limited hardware is challenging. Models may exceed available memory, and selecting quantization methods and bit widths requires specialist expertise. OneComp is an open-source Python library for resource-adaptive post-training quantization. With a single command, it detects available GPU memory, assigns layer-wise bit widths using AutoBit, performs quantization and error correction, evaluates the result, and saves the compressed model. OneComp incorporates Fujitsu\u2019s latest model compression technologies, including Quantization Error Propagation (QEP) and JointQ. This talk will introduce how these techniques help preserve model quality at low precision and explain OneComp\u2019s approach to making LLM compression more accessible.",
