        Case(
            "talk pytorch-day-japan-2026:1343167",
            "From PyTorch to Physical Action: Building Real-Time VLA Inference on Edge Devices\u000AVision-Language-Action (VLA) models enable AI systems to perceive their environment, understand instructions, and perform physical actions; however, deploying VLA models on edge devices requires more than just getting inference running. Real-world systems have to satisfy strict requirements concerning latency, memory, power, thermal behavior, reliability, and security.\u000A\u000AThe talk describes a complete process for moving from a PyTorch VLA model to real-time on-device inference using torch.export and ExecuTorch on ARM-based edge devices. The deployment pipeline includes model optimization, quantization, hardware acceleration, and runtime execution.\u000ASystematic examines the entire perception-to-action process, measuring end-to-end latency, memory usage, power consumption, sustained performance, thermal behavior, and task success. The presentation examines how various optimization techniques and hardware acceleration affect real-time performance.\u000A\u000AThe aim is to develop a practical method for determining when a PyTorch VLA model is ready for real-time Physical AI, moving beyond the simple criterion of \"it runs\" to \"it responds, performs, and acts reliably on the edge.\"",
