        Case(
            "talk pytorch-day-japan-2026:1361901",
            "Where Do RL Environments Come From? Turning Real Data into Tasks, Rewards and Training\u000AFrontier labs post-train models across thousands of RL environments. At their core, these environments expose two things: tasks for models to solve and verifiers that determine whether they succeed. The challenge is scaling both: generating diverse, high-quality tasks from real-world data and building robust verifiers that provide reliable rewards. Yet very little of this work is being done openly at scale.\u000AWe walk through four key decisions in building RL environments: choosing domains with real, verifiable data; turning that data into tasks with controlled difficulty; designing robust rewards that resist hacking; and packaging everything with OpenEnv and Harbor for scalable training and evaluation.\u000AWe then explore how these environments integrate with TRL for GRPO training, including agents running behind a proxy, and share practical examples across coding, games, multilingual OCR and speech, design, biology, and more, highlighting how the environments were built and what training showed.\u000AAll environments and recipes are open in FineEnvs: https://huggingface.co/FineEnvs",
